SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia (Styliotis)\, Kefalos
LOCATION:Kefalos\, Kos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The biggest village panigiri on Kos: the shepherds of Kefalos\, the old capital at the far west\, cook boiled goat with pilaf in huge cauldrons and serve it free after the liturgy on the 15th\, with dancing to island music on the square the night before and after. Kefalos also runs a fish festival in the first half of August. Parking in the village is tight\; use the road below and walk up.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kos/#kefalos-panigiri-of-panagia-styliotis-kefalos
